## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical implementation of multi-tenant isolation in analytics environments, specifically testing knowledge of data-layer controls, IAM scoping, performance optimization, and automated validation mechanisms. It demonstrates understanding of defense-in-depth principles in shared cloud resources.

## Key Concepts

- BigQuery isolation patterns: per-tenant datasets vs. Row-Level Security
- Authorized views and security policy implementation
- IAM role-based access controls with least privilege
- CI/CD validation using synthetic tenant simulation
- Performance optimization with per-tenant BI Engine reservations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo CI script sketch for synthetic tenant validation
const validateTenantIsolation = async () => {
  // Provision synthetic tenant
  await createSyntheticTenant();
  // Test cross-tenant access attempts
  await attemptCrossTenantQueries();
  // Validate isolation enforcement
  await verifyAccessControls();
  // Rollback on failure
  if (!isolationValidated) await rollback();
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end thinking for tenant-scoped data retention across multiple services with auditability and rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Data tagging and lineage across Storage, BigQuery, and Pub/Sub
- Tenant-scoped retention policies, TTLs, and legal holds
- IAM Conditions, per-tenant service accounts, and KMS constraints
- Immutable logs and cryptographic attestations for verification
- Rollback procedures and audit verification planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for tenant deletion
function deleteTenant(tenantId) {
  purgePubSub(tenantId);
  deleteStorageObjects(tenantId);
  dropBigQueryPartitions(tenantId);
  verifyDeletion(tenantId);
  generateAuditReport(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, concrete incident response steps for a multi-tenant GCP SaaS, focusing on rapid containment, credential revocation, and rollback with auditable forensics.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation and containment
- Workload Identity and bindings management
- Network controls: NetworkPolicy, Private Service Connect, VPC Service Controls
- Forensics preservation and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: containment workflow
const onExfiltration = () => {
  isolateTenant();
  revokeIdentity();
  blockEgress();
  preserveForensics();
  runSyntheticTests();
  rollbackIfNeeded();
}
```

